    { h: 'Customers see it before you do', d: 'A broken blog post is embarrassing. A wrong price, a zeroed stock count, or an order flipped to the wrong status costs actual money while it stands, and customers hit it first.' },
    { h: 'MCP endpoints are arriving. None ship an undo.', d: 'Giving an agent raw create, update, and delete access to a live store is easy. What matters the moment something goes wrong is being able to reverse it. WP MCP is the safe layer: the same store operations, wrapped in snapshot-first and one-click restore.' },
    { h: 'Undo one change, or the whole session', d: "Every product edit, price change, and order-status update lands in your dashboard with a Restore button next to it. If an agent's entire afternoon went sideways, roll the whole session back in one click." },
